# ─── Compiled Go binaries ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Stray binaries that `go build ./...` drops in the working dir when run from
# an examples subfolder (e.g. `13_train_classifier`, `22_train_mnist`).
# Pick them up by name pattern so we don't accidentally also catch directories.
/[0-9][0-9]_*
!/[0-9][0-9]_*.go
!/[0-9][0-9]_*.md
# Generic compiled artefacts.
*.exe
*.exe~
*.test
*.out
*.prof
*.coverage
coverage.html
coverage.txt

# ─── Go toolchain ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Module cache + downloaded vendor archives are workspace-local; do not commit.
/vendor/
go.work
go.work.sum

# ─── CUDA build artefacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generated PTX is committed under kernels/cuda/embedded/ so users without
# nvcc can still build. Ignore stray ones in tmp dirs.
*.ptx.tmp
*.cubin
*.fatbin

# ─── Datasets / model weight caches ──────────────────────────────────────────
# These are downloaded on first run and can be hundreds of MB to GBs.
/cifar10-cache/
/mnist-cache/
/imagenet-cache/
/coco-cache/
/.cache/
# HuggingFace Hub cache (when HF_HOME isn't set, we write under this default).
/hf-cache/
# Trained checkpoints written by training examples.
/checkpoints/
*.safetensors
*.gguf
# Preserve any reference fixtures kept as test data.
!/testdata/**/*.safetensors
!/testdata/**/*.gguf

# ─── IDE / OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# JetBrains (GoLand) config — keep local, even shared parts can leak personal info.
.idea/
*.iml
# VS Code workspace settings — but keep recommended extensions / settings examples.
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.example.json
# Vim / Emacs swap files.
*.swp
*.swo
*~
# macOS / Linux droppings.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ─── Local environment ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Claude Code per-machine permission settings (absolute paths).
.claude/
.env
.env.local
.envrc

# ─── Generated docs / build outputs ──────────────────────────────────────────
/build/
/dist/
/out/
*.log

# ─── XGo / Go+ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `xgo go` regenerates `.go` files next to `.gop`/`.xgo` sources — keep the
# source files, ignore the generated mirror.
*.gop.go
*.xgo.go
xgo_autogen.go
# ─── Light Studio (Wails v3 + React) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Built binary, Vite output and node modules are regenerated by `wails3 build`;
# the empty dist/.gitkeep stays so `//go:embed all:frontend/dist` compiles
# from a fresh clone. frontend/bindings/ is generated but committed so the
# frontend builds without a wails3 install.
/studio/bin/
/studio/.task/
/studio/frontend/node_modules/
/studio/frontend/dist/*
!/studio/frontend/dist/.gitkeep
